OpenVPN over PrismNet
=====================

These are the scripts for AmiOpenVPN (https://github.com/Telefonorosso/openvpn),
an OpenVPN client for AmigaOS, to run over PrismNet. AmiOpenVPN and its
vpn.device come from that project; they aren't part of PrismNet.

  StartVPN                  starts a connection:
                              Execute OPENVPN:StartVPN OPENVPN:client.ovpn
  PrismNetUp.script         OpenVPN "up": gives interface vpn0 its address
  PrismNetRouteUp.script    OpenVPN "route-up": routes everything through the
                            tunnel (except the way to the server) and uses
                            the name servers the server pushed
  PrismNetDown.script       OpenVPN "route-pre-down": undoes both

Put vpn.device in DEVS:Networks, assign OPENVPN: to the drawer with openvpn,
your keys and these scripts, and add to your .ovpn file:

  ifconfig-noexec
  route-noexec
  tun-mtu 1400
  script-security 2
  up OPENVPN:PrismNetUp.script
  route-up OPENVPN:PrismNetRouteUp.script
  route-pre-down OPENVPN:PrismNetDown.script

The manual (PrismNet.guide, chapter "VPN") has the details. The scripts use
C:NetCtl, which the PrismNet installer puts in C:.
